test_connect_2d -- 2D connect far from the origin (Nov 2026)
=======================================================================

QUICK START

  sh run_connect_2d_tests.sh [path-to-lagrit]     7 decks, about 1 s
  open logs/summary.html

WHAT IS TESTED

  connect on a triplane mesh object (2D Delaunay triangulation) of the
  same 400 points, made by make_connect_inputs.py from a fixed random
  number generator, in a 100 x 80 rectangle:

  cd01_origin      a corner at the origin: the reference
  cd02_utm         moved to x 4.0e5, y 3.9e6 (UTM-sized coordinates)
  cd03_negative    moved to x -6.5e5, y -4.2e6
  cd04_y_only      moved to y 3.9e6 only (x starts at 0)
  cd05_yz_plane    in the plane x = 0, moved to y 2.0e5, z 3.0e5
  cd06_xz_plane    in the plane y = 0, moved to x 2.0e5, z 3.0e5
  cd07_square1000  the four corners of a unit square at x = 1000 (the
                   case test/level01/connect_errors records as failing)

  HARD checks, every deck: LaGriT finished with no ERROR; connect left
  no point unconnected; the expected number of triangles (778; 2 for
  cd07); every triangle with positive area and the same orientation in
  its plane; every edge shared by one or two triangles; every vertex
  used. cd02-cd06 must also give exactly the triangles of cd01_origin,
  vertex number for vertex number.

WHY

  connect (2D) starts from a large triangle enclosing the points
  (src/make_bigtri_lg.f). In LaGriT V3.3.4 and earlier its third vertex
  was placed at 1.01 times the centre coordinate of the points. Far from
  the origin that is far outside the box (4,000 m away for a 100 m box
  at x = 400,000), the triangle no longer encloses the points, every
  point fails and connect makes no triangles. Now the old place is kept
  when the box of the points contains the origin, so those meshes are
  unchanged, and otherwise the vertex is offset by 0.005 of the box
  size. On such a LaGriT cd02, cd03, cd05, cd06 and cd07 fail; cd01 and
  cd04 pass (cd04: the x offset decides, and x starts at 0).

FILES

  make_connect_inputs.py   writes cd01-cd06 .pts (AVS points) into WORK
  cd*.lgi                  the decks
  check_connect_2d.py      the checker (Python 3, standard library)
  run_connect_2d_tests.sh  the runner; work/ and logs/ are rewritten
